From 6391395f567154871c34637b252a565b3105f644 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:20:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: name the kernel patches that give
 HDR10PLUS_VSIF

The kernel side is the property in DRM (linux-9980) and one backend per
driver: amdgpu (linux-9981) and i915 and xe (linux-9982, over HDMI only
where the HDMI vendor InfoFrame signals no HDMI VIC or 3D, so not at
2160p24, 25 or 30, where the driver refuses it and the output stays
HDR10). The comment named an older numbering. No code changes.
---
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/HDR10PlusOutput.h | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/HDR10PlusOutput.h b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/HDR10PlusOutput.h
index f030c15..7f56338 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/HDR10PlusOutput.h
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/HDR10PlusOutput.h
@@ -28,8 +28,10 @@ namespace GBM
  * the HDR one, and change it with a flip and never with a change of mode, gives its connectors
  * HDR10PLUS_VSIF: a blob of the 27 bytes of its payload (KODI::UTILS::HDR10PLUS), 0 for none.
  * The Hades patches give it: nvidia-open-kernel-modules-9020 (Turing, Ampere and Ada over HDMI,
- * Ada over DisplayPort, T239 and Blackwell over both), linux-9980 (amdgpu) and linux-9981
- * (i915 and xe). A driver refuses, in the commit, what it cannot send.
+ * Ada over DisplayPort, T239 and Blackwell over both), and linux-9980 (the property, in DRM) with
+ * linux-9981 (amdgpu, DCN: HDMI and DisplayPort) and linux-9982 (i915 and xe: HDMI, where no HDMI
+ * VIC or 3D is signalled, so not at 2160p24, 25 or 30). A driver refuses, in the commit, what it
+ * cannot send.
  *
  * The payload of a frame goes out only while the HDR of its video is signalled as PQ (HDR10:
  * HDR10+ is HDR10 and its metadata), the display declares HDR10+ (its HDR10+ vendor-specific
